  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 200 AM CDT Thu Oct 22 2026\n\nThe weak disturbance has made its way inland, bringing in those \nisolated showers which provided some relief from the heat this \nafternoon. There is still a chance for showers but that will \nultimately remain near to offshore for this evening.\n\nThe weather pattern over the South Texas region is expected to \nremain relatively calm throughout the rest of the forecast period. \nThis is mainly due to influence from ridging conditions over the \narea, keeping temperatures near or above the typical seasonal \naverage. Conditions this weekend will be slightly drier after that \nlow moves through the area.\n\nGlancing ahead mid to late next week, models are hinting at chances \nof a possible front moving through the South Texas region. \nConfidence remains low at this time but will continued to be \nmonitored as the week progresses. \n\nMinor coastal flooding still remains likely through the beginning of \nnext week with more easterly flow of winds. Swells are elevated \naround 7 to 8 seconds, which can pose a moderate rip current risk.",
